y \sin \theta & =x+\frac{35\left(\sin ^2 \theta-1\right)}{\cos \theta} \\
y \sin \theta & =x+\frac{35(-\cos 2 \theta)}{\cos \theta} \\
y \sin \theta & =x-35 \cos \theta
\end{aligned}

Hence, option (2) is correct.

